# Redirect URL normalization - ensure canonical paths
#
# All retirement/migration redirects below use the "!" force flag. Without
# it, Netlify lets an existing static file at the same path win over a
# redirect — and content-pipeline's automated daily job has no awareness of
# these permanent retirements, so it can (and on 2026-10-05, did) republish
# a fresh article under a slug that was deliberately redirected just days
# earlier, silently shadowing the redirect with the new prerendered page
# (confirmed live: /destinations/italy/ served a brand-new "Traveling in
# Italy" article instead of 301'ing to the Rome restaurant guide, even
# though the rule below was present and correct). Forcing these redirects
# makes that class of bug impossible regardless of what content-pipeline
# republishes later — see CHANGELOG 2026-10-12.
/destinations/abudhabi /destinations/abu-dhabi 301!

# New York's static page (1 genuine hotel, below the usual 3-hotel minimum
# for a standalone article) was consolidated into the existing
# DB-driven holiday-season article, which already covers the same one
# real hotel (The Plaza) plus genuine editorial content — see CHANGELOG
# 2026-10-03.
/destinations/newyork /destinations/new-york-holiday-season-allergy-friendly-hotels 301!
/destinations/new-york /destinations/new-york-holiday-season-allergy-friendly-hotels 301!

# Migrated from static hotel pages to DB-driven restaurant articles
# (2026-10-03) — these pages were restaurant-only (hotels: [] in the old
# static file), so under the new architecture their content lives under
# /restaurants/ rather than /destinations/. See CHANGELOG.
/destinations/athens /restaurants/athens 301!
/destinations/stockholm /restaurants/stockholm 301!

# Italy's static page's real content was entirely Rome gluten-free
# restaurants (despite the page's title claiming Florence/Milan/Naples
# coverage too, none of which ever had real listed evidence) — migrated
# to the Rome restaurant article rather than kept as a separate thin page.
/destinations/italy /restaurants/gluten-free-eating-in-rome 301!

# Warm Winter Destinations claimed coverage of Madeira, Hurghada, the
# Canary Islands, and Israel, but only ever had real listed evidence for
# Israel (1 hotel, 2 restaurants) — the other three regions' hotel arrays
# were always empty, so their "verified" copy never actually rendered a
# single hotel/restaurant card (MultiRegionHotelsSection returns null for
# any region with zero hotels). Migrated the one real region to two much
# richer, fully re-verified DB articles (Eilat hotels, Tel Aviv
# restaurants, cross-linked to each other) instead of keeping this page.
/destinations/warm-winter-destinations /destinations/traveling-to-eilat-food-allergy-friendly-guide 301!

